<Layout title="Evidence & sources"><div class="wrap"><header class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">Know what is established</p><h1>A guide with receipts.</h1><p class="lede">Board documentation, implementation records and device observations answer different questions. This guide keeps them separate.</p></header><article class="prose"><h2>Read the evidence level</h2><ul><li><strong>Documented capability:</strong> an authoritative vendor or chip source establishes support or wiring.</li><li><strong>Implemented:</strong> an app uses the capability. A build proves compilation, not physical behavior.</li><li><strong>Observed on device:</strong> a dated serial or physical check establishes what was actually seen during that run.</li><li><strong>Explore / UNKNOWN:</strong> an idea or unresolved detail that needs a diagnostic or explicit device check.</li></ul><h2>Repository evidence</h2><ul><li><a href="https://github.com/cmwen/FNK0104B/blob/main/knowledge/board.md">Board facts</a> and <a href="https://github.com/cmwen/FNK0104B/blob/main/knowledge/pins.yaml">verified pin inventory</a>.</li><li><a href="https://github.com/cmwen/FNK0104B/blob/main/knowledge/references.md">Source index</a> with Freenove schematic, specification and tutorials.</li><li><a href="https://github.com/cmwen/FNK0104B/blob/main/docs/hardware.md">Hardware observations</a> and <a href="https://github.com/cmwen/FNK0104B/tree/main/test/hardware">dated device records</a>.</li><li><a href="https://github.com/cmwen/FNK0104B/blob/main/docs/monitor-readiness.md">Monitor readiness</a> and <a href="https://github.com/cmwen/FNK0104B/blob/main/docs/monitor-setup.md">local bridge setup</a>.</li><li><a href="https://github.com/cmwen/FNK0104B/blob/main/scripts/README.md">Screenshot and preview tools</a>. The main monitor screenshot is LCD readback. Recorder and alternate monitor states are host-rendered drawing code with sample data.</li></ul><h2>Authoritative technical references</h2><ul><li><a href="https://docs.freenove.com/projects/fnk0104/en/latest/fnk0104/codes/MAIN/Freenove_ESP32S3_Display.html">Freenove display model comparison</a>.</li><li><a href="https://docs.espressif.com/projects/esp-idf/en/v6.0/esp32s3/api-reference/peripherals/usb_device.html">Espressif USB device stack and HID example</a>.</li><li><a href="https://github.com/espressif/esp-sr">Espressif speech recognition</a> and <a href="https://docs.espressif.com/projects/esp-sr/en/latest/esp32s3/benchmark/README.html">ESP32-S3 benchmarks</a>.</li><li><a href="https://developer.chrome.com/docs/capabilities/bluetooth">Chrome Web Bluetooth support and requirements</a>.</li><li><a href="https://developer.android.com/develop/connectivity/usb/host">Android USB host capability</a>.</li><li><a href="https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/core/">PlatformIO Core CLI</a>.</li></ul><h2>Unresolved board details</h2><p>The physical PCB revision, fitted touch-controller suffix and amplifier part, original factory partition layout, battery calibration and current attached expansion devices remain UNKNOWN. HID host compatibility, custom ML models and deep-sleep wake are not implemented or verified here.</p><p>This guide reflects repository evidence through 4 October 2026. When you verify new hardware behavior, update the knowledge files and the relevant app's record before extending a capability claim.</p></article></div></Layout>
